From: Haiku PostgreSQL port <user@haiku>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 03:58:00 +0000
Subject: Preserve IEEE negative zero in float4/float8 input on Haiku

Haiku strtod("-0") and strtof("-0") return +0 (signbit clear). C99 and
PostgreSQL require a signed zero so float PK/FK updates on -0 vs 0 work.
If the scanned token starts with ASCII '-' and the value is zero, flip
the sign. Official foreign_key regress then passes.

--- a/src/backend/utils/adt/float.c
+++ b/src/backend/utils/adt/float.c
@@ -210,6 +210,11 @@
 	errno = 0;
 	val = strtof(num, &endptr);
 
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+	if (val == 0.0f && *num == 45)
+		val = -val;
+#endif
+
 	/* did we not see anything that looks like a double? */
 	if (endptr == num || errno != 0)
 	{
@@ -416,6 +421,15 @@
 	errno = 0;
 	val = strtod(num, &endptr);
 
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+	/*
+	 * Haiku strtod("-0") returns +0.  C99 requires a signed zero.  If the
+	 * scanned token started with - and the value is zero, restore the sign.
+	 */
+	if (val == 0.0 && *num == 45)
+		val = -val;
+#endif
+
 	/* did we not see anything that looks like a double? */
 	if (endptr == num || errno != 0)
 	{
